<title>ITALY: Italy's Reno De Medici 1996 cons profit up.</title>
<headline>Italy's Reno De Medici 1996 cons profit up.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			 11.7  vs   7.1</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		    19.1  vs  14.5</p>
<p>    Cons gross operating profit	 40.7  vs  43.9</p>
<p>    Cons net revenue		     237.4  vs 284.3</p>
<p>    Amortisations			   20.0  vs  17.9</p>
<p>    Net financial charges		  2.2  vs   6.8</p>
<p>    Parent net revenue		   211.0  vs 260.0</p>
<p>    Parent gross operating profit     35.5  vs  35.6</p>
<p>    Parent co pretax profit	     17.2  vs  11.2</p>
<p>    Parent co net profit		  11.0  vs   6.9</p>
<p>Note - Cardboard and packaging group Reno De Medici SpA made its debut on the Milan bourse in July 1996. It said in a statement after a board meeting the group's results were &quot;more than satisfying&quot; given the generally low demand and flat output trend in the sector.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
